base-files (2) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * Ship /etc/gettytab and /etc/ttys for the console login.
  * Set the clock with ntpdate at boot. apt update waits up to 30 seconds for it.
    ntpdate logs to syslog, not the console.
  * Accounts live in OpenDirectory. rc starts opendirectoryd after syslogd.
  * /etc/shells lists only /bin/sh, the one shell installed.
  * rc starts opendirectoryd again if it exits.
  * base-files 1 can't be upgraded to 2: install a new image.
  * rc sets the clock to the newest log or package time before syslogd starts.
  * rc starts auditd after syslogd, if it is installed. auditd checks in
    the audit control port that init made, and audit -i starts the trail.
  * rc.shutdown closes the audit trail before a reboot or halt. init 3 runs it.

